From 57ed3b7b770714cbef1536debd8c8197b9071cb5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: InMys <dev@inmys.ru>
Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 19:49:35 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] drm/rockchip: dw-mipi-dsi2: fix PHY_SYS_RATIO off by a factor
 of two

PHY_SYS_RATIO_MAN_CFG is programmed as phy_hstx_clk / sys_clk with
sys_clk taken from clk_get_rate(), which on RK3588 is CLK_DSIHOST0 at
351MHz. The controller wants twice that. With the driver's value the
link never leaves stopstate: OBS_FSM_STATUS sits in state 9 with its
counter saturated and PHY_STATUS reads 0x001f1e00.

Auto calculation mode lets the controller measure the ratio itself.
Its SYS_RATIO_AUTO against what this code writes, CLK_DSIHOST0 at
351MHz, 4 lanes:

  lane rate    driver      SYS_RATIO_AUTO
  891 Mbps     0x289e      0x513b
  220 Mbps     0x0a07      0x140f
  198 Mbps     0x0906      0x120d
  144 Mbps     0x0690      0x0d21

exactly x2 at every rate, while IPI_RATIO_AUTO matches the driver's
IPI_RATIO to the last bit or two (0x18002 against 0x18000), so the
phy_hstx_clk side of the ratio is right and the sys_clk side is not.
The same factor of two was reported for a DSI panel on RK3588 on
dri-devel [1].

Doubling only the ratio fixes the link at 198 and 891 Mbps. Doubling
LP2HS/HS2LP instead, with the original ratio, does not, so it is the
ratio itself that matters and not merely longer LP/HS transitions.

sys_clk is also used for the escape clock divider; that is left alone,
so phy_lptx_clk stays within the 20MHz limit whichever way the factor
of two is explained.

Link: https://www.mail-archive.com/dri-devel@lists.freedesktop.org/msg527842.html [1]
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/rockchip/dw-mipi-dsi2-rockchip.c | 7 +++++--
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/rockchip/dw-mipi-dsi2-rockchip.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/rockchip/dw-mipi-dsi2-rockchip.c
index ee38e48..0f81a2f 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/rockchip/dw-mipi-dsi2-rockchip.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/rockchip/dw-mipi-dsi2-rockchip.c
@@ -636,9 +636,12 @@ static void dw_mipi_dsi2_phy_ratio_cfg(struct dw_mipi_dsi2 *dsi2)
 		     PHY_IPI_RATIO(tmp));
 
 	/*
-	 * SYS_RATIO_MAN_CFG = MIPI_DCPHY_HSCLK_Freq / MIPI_DCPHY_HSCLK_Freq
+	 * SYS_RATIO_MAN_CFG = MIPI_DCPHY_HSCLK_Freq / SYS_CLK_Freq, where the
+	 * controller counts its sys clock at half the rate of the clock it is
+	 * fed: SYS_RATIO_AUTO, measured by the controller itself, comes out
+	 * at exactly twice this ratio against clk_get_rate(sys_clk).
 	 */
-	tmp = DIV_ROUND_CLOSEST_ULL(phy_hsclk << 16, sys_clk);
+	tmp = DIV_ROUND_CLOSEST_ULL(phy_hsclk << 16, sys_clk / 2);
 	regmap_write(dsi2->regmap, DSI2_PHY_SYS_RATIO_MAN_CFG,
 		     PHY_SYS_RATIO(tmp));
 }
